{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-09-22T04:53:15.143Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"0cc560e29dd3d55e0c5a6361","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"ops-wwu1"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Certify pm CLI 2026.9.21 and move onto the canonical pm-ops merge-driver, lint and duplication gates"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Wave 2026-09-22, companion epic pm-cli-website-5s6z. pm-ops IS the canonical source: it already ships the launcher prepare-merge-driver.ts, pm-ops/eslint and pm-ops/duplication, so this wave for pm-ops is (a) pin @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.9.21 + pm-changelog 2026.9.18 in devDependencies, (b) add the CI 'pm merge install' step and --require-merge-drivers on the health command, (c) absorb Dependabot #117 (jscpd 4.3.0 -> 5.2.1) and #116 (@types/node), (d) verify and fix scripts/duplication.ts against the real jscpd 5 programmatic API, widen the optional peer to ^4.3.0 || ^5.2.1, prove both majors report identical clone pairs and install without ERESOLVE, (e) verify eslint 10.x runs cleanly."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Task"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["certify","multi-agent","pm-cli-2026.9.21","quality"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-09-22T04:53:15.143Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-22T04:53:15.143Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pi-agent"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"package.json + package-lock.json pin @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.9.21 and pm-changelog 2026.9.18 in devDependencies; peerDependencies floor unchanged; CI runs pm merge install before pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers; health exits 0 locally; jscpd 5.2.1 devDependency; duplication.ts works against the real jscpd 5 programmatic API with 100/100/100/100 coverage and real tests (no mocks of jscpd); optional peer jscpd widened to ^4.3.0 || ^5.2.1; README Consumers states both majors supported; functional proof in jscpd-proof scratch projects: runDuplicationGate/analyzeDuplication report the same clone pairs on a real fleet .ts tree with jscpd@4.3.0 and jscpd@5.2.1; npm install of the built tarball with jscpd 5.2.1 has no ERESOLVE; release:check exits 0 after changelog:full"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"57f1e11c4d140536e6e70aebf85ef6c404ce018ed78e9fcd0ee01f5ad7e9486c","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"aa717ae5c67711754f162076c950677ae58587550b06b8cc623581beb9e9a9cb"}
