{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-09-22T05:02:21.449Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"0cc560e29dd3d55e0c5a6361","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-22T05:02:21.449Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-09-22T05:02:21.449Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"jscpd 5 has NO Node.js API: node_modules/jscpd@5.2.1 and 5.3.1 contain only run-jscpd.js + platform-map.js (Rust binary wrapper; README: 'Programming API ... no Node.js API' for v5). Rewrote duplication.ts to dispatch on installed major: v4 programmatic API (unchanged semantics) vs v5 binary run via node run-jscpd.js --reporters json, parsed + validated fail-closed. Percentage now computed as duplicatedLines/totalLines*100 for both majors (v4 rounded to 1 decimal, masking e.g. 0.44% as 0.4). v5 sources = in-scope matched files (v5's statistics.total.sources drops sub-minTokens files which cannot hold a minTokens clone; garbage files are still analyzed, verified)."}]}],"before_hash":"2a13cbc053f14816f3a1da3c70200c2bbca0fcf81b514736eef2e136ef295b8f","after_hash":"978e14eaa672b15d6f4741649ab21e4742bdd06cd195bfefb199c2c5c0febdcf","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"f8af95235b8595dfb3eed4c04f19e87e9e29ef7203a26fd04643ff673cf3beee"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-09-22T19:12:44.945Z","author":"pi-glm-pmops","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"9c4cae7a83d7e1c37693030b","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-09-22T19:12:44.945Z","author":"pi-glm-pmops","text":"Root cause of npm test failure: the jscpd peer dependency \"^4.3.0 || ^5.2.1\" contains pipe characters (|) which the pm CLI rejects as shell metacharacters during pm package install (error code extension_dependency_version_unsafe). Fixed by changing the peer to \">=4.3.0 <6.0.0\" which covers both jscpd 4.x and 5.x without any shell metacharacters. npm test now passes 433/433 (2 skipped), release:check exits 0 with 100/100/100/100 coverage, pm health --strict-exit exits 0. Also updated README Consumers section to state both jscpd majors are supported and show the new version range."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-22T19:12:44.945Z"}],"before_hash":"978e14eaa672b15d6f4741649ab21e4742bdd06cd195bfefb199c2c5c0febdcf","after_hash":"7d3164a25722b9d9f114aa394c7ffe0c29cc5595cdf387862fb5fa25167ed004","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"673ff1c3abda897e9c8c439ba3957731861a621e9ae636a216c015d94961b925"}
